---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base
  title="How We Calculate — Methodology"
  description="Detailed mathematical formulas, tax bracket assumptions, and CDR bank rate rules behind Howloop's Australian financial calculators."
>
  <div class="hl-wrap hl-prose-wrap">
    <article class="hl-prose">
      <h1>Calculation Methodology</h1>
      <p>
        Every calculator on {SITE.name} uses deterministic client-side mathematics. Below we document the exact equations, rounding rules, and data boundaries used across our tools.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Take-Home Pay &amp; Income Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Our salary calculator applies the Australian resident individual income tax rates (Stage 3 tax cuts effective from FY 2024–25 through FY 2025–26 and FY 2026–27):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>$0 – $18,200:</strong> Nil (0%)</li>
        <li><strong>$18,201 – $45,000:</strong> 16 cents for each $1 over $18,200</li>
        <li><strong>$45,001 – $135,000:</strong> $4,288 plus 30 cents for each $1 over $45,000</li>
        <li><strong>$135,001 – $190,000:</strong> $31,288 plus 37 cents for each $1 over $135,000</li>
        <li><strong>$190,001 and over:</strong> $51,638 plus 45 cents for each $1 over $190,000</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The standard 2.0% Medicare levy is applied alongside Low Income Tax Offset (LITO) phase-out rules and statutory Superannuation Guarantee (12.0% of Ordinary Time Earnings).
      </p>

      <h2>2. Compound Interest &amp; Mortgage Offset Models</h2>
      <p>
        Compound interest projections model monthly compounding with contributions credited at the end of each period. Mortgage offset comparisons model daily interest reduction on the net principal balance (<code>Loan Balance − Offset Balance</code>) compared against the post-tax return of a taxable savings account at the user's effective marginal tax rate.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Consumer Data Right (CDR) Banking Snapshots</h2>
      <p>
        Our rate collector fetches public product detail endpoints from the Australian Government CDR register. Only unambiguous base variable rates (`DEPOSIT_RATE` / `BASE`) and full-coverage dollar tiers are automatically modelled in calculator pickers; conditional bonus tiers are displayed separately for context.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
